<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Miangul Jahanzeb</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1908">1908</a>–<a href="/years/1987">1987</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Miangul Jahanzeb was the second and last Wali of Swat, ruling from 1949 until the state was merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> in 1969. The son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miangul-abdul-wadud">Miangul Abdul Wadud</a>, he spent much of the state's revenue on schools, hospitals and colleges centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saidu-sharif">Saidu Sharif</a>, and Swat became known for its order and education among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> of the north-west.</p></div>
